course: dictionary
lesson: 11146
title: Wildebeest on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wildebeest is a large African antelope with curved horns, a long face, a mane and a beard. Another name for it is gnu.
explain: Wildebeest live in big herds on the grasslands. «Each year more than a million wildebeest, with zebras and gazelles, follow the rain and fresh grass.» They travel long distances to find fresh grass and water.
explain: Use context to work out new words. «On the real savanna zebras, giraffes and wildebeest graze side by side.» Zebras and giraffes are eating, so graze must mean eat grass.
fact: A wildebeest is a large African antelope, also called a gnu.
fact: The plural of wildebeest is wildebeest or wildebeests.
fact: Wildebeest live in big herds on grasslands and travel long distances for fresh grass and water.
fact: «The Serengeti has millions of wildebeest but only a few thousand lions.» Wildebeest are prey for lions, cheetahs and hyenas.
fact: «Graze» means to eat grass while moving slowly across the land.
exercise: In «Each year more than a million wildebeest... follow the rain and fresh grass», what do the wildebeest follow? | Cars on the road | *The rain and fresh grass | The stars at night | Crocodiles in the river
exercise: Another name for the wildebeest is the | *Gnu | Zebra | Giraffe
exercise: Wildebeest live in big herds on the grasslands. What does herd mean? | A river crossing | A single animal living alone | A type of tall grass | *A large group of animals living together
test: In «zebras, giraffes and wildebeest graze side by side», what does graze mean? | Run very fast | Sleep in trees | *Eat grass | Swim across rivers
test: «The Serengeti has millions of wildebeest but only a few thousand lions.» Why are there more wildebeest than lions? | Lions are too big to hunt | Lions live only in rivers | Wildebeest can fly away from lions | *Each lion needs to eat many prey animals
exam: Which feature belongs to a wildebeest? | Feathers | Scales | *Curved horns | Wings
